\section*{Results}

\subsection*{A longitudinal prediction atlas across haematological disease}
The sealed first-line source contained 37,557 patients, of whom 37,531 had
released overall-survival membership and a supervised split before
outcome-specific eligibility. Patients were assigned to 24 fine disease
cohorts nested within 10 broader disease groups. Cohort size ranged from \placeholder{minimum} to
\placeholder{maximum}, creating a natural test of performance under data
scarcity. The approved primary panel contains 69 outcomes covering disease control, treatment
trajectory, infection, organ toxicity, haematological toxicity, acute care,
subsequent malignancy, and survival. Each outcome was evaluated at 30, 60, 90,
180, 365, and 730 days when adequate events and follow-up were available.

