\subsection*{Sequence models versus task-specific tabular learning}
For each estimable fine cohort, outcome and horizon, the planned tabular
comparison fits XGBoost to locked pre-index EHR feature matrices and evaluates
it on the same held-out patients as OPERA. Registry-augmented models and
established clinical scores require separate, explicitly reported complete-case
populations. The feature-matrix and risk-set alignment are still being audited;
no OPERA--XGBoost superiority claim follows from the neural tuning screen.
\placeholder{Insert verified matched tabular predictions, hierarchical
OPERA--XGBoost contrast and forest plot.}

The purpose of this comparison is not to require one model class to dominate
every task. Instead, we estimate where temporal representation, cross-cohort
sharing, or cross-outcome sharing changes the performance frontier, and where
a task-specific tabular model remains the appropriate benchmark.

